.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-media - Upload and manage public media library images


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad media [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Upload and manage images in your public media library.

.PP
Media library files are hosted on Gumroad's public CDN, which is the only host custom product landing pages and profile pages can display images from. Use \fBmedia upload\fR to host an image and embed the returned URL in page HTML (see \fBgumroad pages push\fR). Files from \fBgumroad files upload\fR are stored privately and will fail page moderation — they cannot be used on pages.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for media


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad media upload ./logo.png
  gumroad media upload ./logo.png --name "Store logo"
  gumroad media list
  gumroad media delete k3n8xq1p9wr2sd4a
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad(1)\fP, \fBgumroad-media-delete(1)\fP, \fBgumroad-media-list(1)\fP, \fBgumroad-media-upload(1)\fP
